These are the items I feel you need to ascend:
blessed ring of levitation
blessed bag of holding - for carrying capacity, also protects scrolls and
potions from fire traps
shield of reflection
speed boots - two attacks/turn, and can run away
Named weapon enchanted above +5
All armor and weapons rustproof
lots of food- 20-25 rations (get by polypiling)
Holy water and remove curse scrolls
Along with cold, fire, shock, etc. resistance (which can be obtained by
eating corpses), magic resistance. This protects you from polymorph traps.
Can be gotten from GDSM or cloak of magic resistance. You said you had blue
dragon scale mail and a +5 cloak of displacement. If you step on a poly.
trap (and you will find one), bye bye cloak.
Intrinsic tel. control: can be gotten by reverse genociding tengu's. Makes
escaping Gehennom easier.
Intrinsic teleport: Get it from nymph or lep. corpses. You can move around 
in the mazes a lot faster if you have this & tel. control.

Other things:
blessed ring of conflict
  "     spellbook of magic mapping (Finding Vlad a lot easier with this)
  "     AOLS
  "     helm of telepathy: when you kill Moloch's priest, you lose telepathy
  "     gauntlets of power - for melee and carrying capacity
  "     spellbook of identify- Can ID worthless gems of every color, then
        all other gems are valuable.
About the only things you seem to find in Gehennom are wands & scrolls
of create monster and teleportation, so you should have everything before
you get there. Rember the AOLS in Vlad's Tower.
Usually by the time you get to Gehennom, you are pretty much invincible.
Your character sounds a lot like that. Remember that the most common death is
by stupidity: falling into a moat or something. The next common is the Touch of
Death by the Wizard. The best way to kill him, IMO, is to use the heaviest
damaging weapon (in your case, Mjollnir) vs. the quick kill method (Vorpal
Blade or wand of death). Good luck.

